</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;">
<span id="S4.SS5.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:327.8pt;--ltx-bg-color:#BFBFBF;">
<span id="S4.SS5.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p3.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Answer to RQ3:</span> Scalpel outperforms all the existing methods with the shortest average time to generate each valid test input model (42.19 seconds) and detect each automotive DL framework bug (568.42 seconds). Furthermore, it achieves the highest operator coverage (100%) and model component coverage (82%).</span>
</span></span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.6. </span>RQ4: Ablation Study</h3>

<div id="S4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Scalpel heuristically selects and mutates model component (Section <a href="#S3.SS3.SSS2" title="3.3.2. Model Component Selection ‣ 3.3. Test Input Model Generation ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Scalpel: Automotive Deep Learning Framework Testing via Assembling Model Components" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3.2</span></a> and <a href="#S3.SS3.SSS3" title="3.3.3. Model Component Mutation ‣ 3.3. Test Input Model Generation ‣ 3. Methodology ‣ Scalpel: Automotive Deep Learning Framework Testing via Assembling Model Components" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3.3</span></a>). In this section, we set up three baselines to evaluate the contribution of heuristic guidance. Among them, the first is <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Scalpel_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Scalpel_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, which randomly selects operator during mutation and only heuristically selects the model component. The second is <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Scalpel_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Scalpel_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>, which randomly selects the model component and only mutates the model component heuristically. The last is <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Random" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Random</annotation></semantics></math>, which disables all heuristic guidance, and selects and mutates model components randomly. All baselines are executed on the same workstation for six hours separately. The experimental result is shown in Table <a href="#S4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 4.6. RQ4: Ablation Study ‣ 4. Evaluation ‣ Scalpel: Automotive Deep Learning Framework Testing via Assembling Model Components" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. The first column in the table represents the method names, while the second and third columns indicate the number of crashes and NaN &amp; inconsistency bugs detected, respectively. The experimental results show that <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Scalpel_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Scalpel_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> detects seven crashes and 16 NaN &amp; inconsistency bugs, outperforming <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Random" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Random</annotation></semantics></math>, which highlights the importance of heuristic model component selection. <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Scalpel_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Scalpel_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> detects eight crashes and 13 NaN &amp; Inconsistency bugs, surpassing <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Random" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Random</annotation></semantics></math>, demonstrating the contribution of heuristic model component mutation. <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Scalpel" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Scalpel</annotation></semantics></math> outperforms both <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Scalpel_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Scalpel_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Scalpel_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Scalpel_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>, showing that heuristic guidance in model component selection and mutation can work together effectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6. </span>Bug Detection Effectiveness in Ablation Study</figcaption>
